# Cloudflare security headers.
#
# This file replaces vercel.json, which Cloudflare ignores completely (same way
# .htaccess only works on Apache). Lives in public/ so Vite copies it into dist/
# at build time. Rules are a direct port of what was in vercel.json.
#
# ⚠️ TEST AFTER DEPLOYING. A CSP that's too strict breaks things silently — open
# the live site, press Cmd+Opt+J for the console, and look for red
# "Refused to..." errors. See the note on style-src below.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; frame-src https://www.planyo.com https://planyo.com https://maps.google.com https://www.google.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://formspree.io; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# NOTE ON style-src 'unsafe-inline':
# vercel.json did NOT include 'unsafe-inline' in style-src. This codebase uses
# React inline styles (style={{...}}) heavily — every one of those becomes an
# inline style attribute, which CSP blocks without 'unsafe-inline'. Without it
# the site renders with large parts of its styling missing.
#
# It has been added here so the site works. It is a genuine (small) weakening of
# the policy: it permits inline styles, not inline scripts, so the XSS risk is
# limited. Removing it properly would mean refactoring the inline styles into
# CSS classes — worth doing eventually, not before launch.
